{
  "scope": "Experimental prototype: 6 proposed starter cards and 6 reward directions, not a finalized 10-reward set. Live gameplay untouched.",
  "rules": "2×3, occupied row/column activate once, complete lines clear; one card per turn; emergency immediately recycles under existing rules.",
  "checks": [
    "Prototype preserves cross activation and complete-line-only clearing",
    "Prototype correctly converts credit into block and consumes it",
    "Scry has no choice in any of 720 initial six-card deck orders",
    "100-turn no-attack stall loop is legal and preserves health",
    "Cover then seven emergency arrows wins all 720 first-encounter starting orders at full health",
    "Area trades focused damage for greater total damage across multiple enemies",
    "Concentration can prevent an urgent attack while area cannot",
    "Current bleed ticks before counterattack, so lethal bleed also prevents the immediate attack",
    "Bleed keeps dealing damage after its card disappears",
    "Kill-heal can be preferred at lower nominal damage",
    "Heal card is not a universal replacement for stronger killing attack",
    "Partial spend creates damage-versus-reserve tradeoff",
    "Half-spend has a concrete advantage when protected boss cannot take overflow",
    "Reducing emergency bleed to 3 restores a real immediate-kill tradeoff",
    "Existing grid order already changes damage and saved momentum",
    "Recall exchanges hand composition without playing a second card or changing turn rules"
  ],
